[1mCoverage.[22m Rather than trusting a hand-written input list, I built a [38;5;10mgcc --coverage[0m copy of the C source in [38;5;10m/tmp[0m and drove it with the test corpus: [1m100% line coverage on all six C files[22m. That found two input classes my initial enumeration missed — [38;5;10mlib.c[0m's [38;5;10mcode % 10 ∈ {7,8,9}[0m paths, and [38;5;10mengine.c[0m's [38;5;10mcase 2[0m trace arm, which needs [38;5;10mclassify[0m to return exactly 2. Both need specific immediates ([38;5;10m0 7 5[0m, [38;5;10m0 8 8[0m) that opcode-shaped random programs essentially never produce. Both matched the C immediately, so they were test-suite gaps, not translation defects. Beyond the suite I ran ~55,000 additional randomized pairs, also all matching.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe one output difference is not a defect.[22m [38;5;10musage()[0m prints [38;5;10margv[0][0m, which is by definition the path of whichever binary ran. The harness replaces each program's own path with [38;5;10m<PROG>[0m and compares every other byte exactly.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mThe interesting part[22m is what the C does that a reasonable translation would get wrong, and that this one gets right. [38;5;10mprocess_a_stream[0m compares a [38;5;10msize_t[0m accumulator against [38;5;10m-0x80000000LL[0m; the conversion makes that condition unconditionally true, so the function returns [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m for every input regardless of the data — [38;5;10mdriver 9 0[0m prints [38;5;10mA:STACK_TOP=-2147483648[0m. [38;5;10mREDUCE[0m pops its operands twice, and since [38;5;10miv_pop[0m leaves [38;5;10m*out[0m untouched on failure, a partially-drained second pass leaves some slots holding first-pass values. [38;5;10mvm_print[0m masks with [38;5;10m& 25[0m instead of [38;5;10m& 31[0m, collapsing distinct trace codes onto the same letter. A negative jump distance sign-extends into a huge [38;5;10msize_t[0m and so always fails the bound check instead of jumping backwards. An empty argv entry parses as the bytecode [38;5;10m0[0m, because [38;5;10mstrtol[0m sets [38;5;10mendptr == nptr[0m which already points at the NUL. All reproduced verbatim.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I also accounted for every branch gcov reports as never taken, so none is left as an open question. Most are provably dead: [38;5;10ma.c[0m's [38;5;10mreturn 6[0m cannot fire because [38;5;10mstate_a[0m starts at 0 and is only ever XORed with [38;5;10mcode << 1[0m, so it stays even forever; the [38;5;10me &&[0m null checks are dead because [38;5;10mstrtol[0m always stores an endptr. The rest are out-of-memory paths. Full detail, including the reasoning for each, is in [38;5;10mtranslation/ERRORS.md[0m.[0m[0m
